{"name":"Pelican Feather","hex":"#e8c3c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pelican","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various seabirds of the family Pelecanidae, having a long bill with a distendable pouch.","A native or resident of the American state of Louisiana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pelican"},{"term":"feather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds, used for flight, swimming, protection and display.","Long hair on the lower legs of a dog or horse, especially a draft horse, notably the Clydesdale breed. Narrowly only the rear hair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or furnish with feathers;  to fletch.","To adorn, as if with feathers; to fringe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pelican","blocks":[{"text":"Pelicans are a genus of large water birds that make up the family Pelecanidae. They are characterized by a long beak and a large throat pouch used for catching prey and draining water from the scooped-up contents before swallowing. They have predominantly pale plumage, except for the brown and Peruvian pelicans. The bills, pouches, and bare facial skin of all pelicans become brightly coloured before the breeding season."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Pelikan_Walvis_Bay.jpg/330px-Pelikan_Walvis_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelican","wikidata":"Q19413"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg/330px-Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather","wikidata":"Q81025"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg/500px-Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg/1280px-Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg/500px-Pelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pelicans at National Zoo, Bangladesh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APelicans_at_National_Zoo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Hammerkopf2.jpg/500px-Hammerkopf2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Hammerkopf2.jpg/1280px-Hammerkopf2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Hammerkopf2.jpg/500px-Hammerkopf2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHammerkopf2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Balaeniceps_rex_-Ueno_Zoo%2C_Tokyo%2C_Japan_-upper_body-8a.jpg/500px-Balaeniceps_rex_-Ueno_Zoo%2C_Tokyo%2C_Japan_-upper_body-8a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Ba